From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:37:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: sun4i-a10-tcon: Add the A733 TCON TV

The A733 has two TCON TVs in its VIDEO_OUT1 block group. They are
channel 1 only TCONs like the R40 TCON TV, with a bus clock, a pixel
clock and a reset, but their registers sit in a power domain that the
power controller switches off when no device claims it.

Add the compatible to the TV branch and allow a power domain.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board with a device tree that
uses this binding; TCON TV1 probes and dtbs_check reports nothing.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/display/allwinner,sun4i-a10-tcon.yaml           | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/allwinner,sun4i-a10-tcon.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/allwinner,sun4i-a10-tcon.yaml
index 724d93b9193b..4cd072fc6041 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/allwinner,sun4i-a10-tcon.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/allwinner,sun4i-a10-tcon.yaml
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@ properties:
       - const: allwinner,sun9i-a80-tcon-tv
       - const: allwinner,sun20i-d1-tcon-lcd
       - const: allwinner,sun20i-d1-tcon-tv
+      - const: allwinner,sun60i-a733-tcon-tv
 
       - items:
           - enum:
@@ -80,6 +81,9 @@ properties:
   dmas:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  power-domains:
+    maxItems: 1
+
   resets:
     anyOf:
       - items:
@@ -254,6 +258,7 @@ allOf:
               - allwinner,sun8i-r40-tcon-tv
               - allwinner,sun9i-a80-tcon-tv
               - allwinner,sun20i-d1-tcon-tv
+              - allwinner,sun60i-a733-tcon-tv
 
     then:
       properties:
